    "end": "She'd had her hair done.",
    "caption": "Enjoy the guests while they last.\n\nVow: 760,000 people, a 23-hour day, one moon, and weddings where everything else disappears. The moment the couple turn to face each other, the guests go, then the chapel, then the hills, and for a minute there's nothing on the planet but the two of them. Everyone comes back afterwards, usually somewhere near the cake. The vicar has stopped taking it personally.\n\nI went to a wedding there. I disappeared at twenty past two and turned up in somebody else's wedding photos.\n\n(The story goes that the bridal veil began as a way to keep the groom from seeing the bride's face until the vows were said. On Vow, it's the groom who can't see anything else.)\n\nWould everything still disappear at yours?"
  },
  "first_comment": "Ron's asked if they can renew them again next spring. Carol's already booked the hairdresser.",
